INT. THE VASQUEZ-LINDEN KITCHEN - SUNDAY NOON

A bright, crowded kitchen. Pots on every burner. A radio plays something with trumpets.

ROSALIND VASQUEZ-LINDEN (50s) chops onions with violent speed. Her husband, GREGORIUS LINDEN (50s), hunts through a drawer for a corkscrew. Their daughter, SELMA (20s), stands in the doorway with a suitcase.

ROSALIND
(without turning)
You're late.

SELMA
The train --

GREGORIUS
(to the drawer)
Where is that blasted thing?

ROSALIND
Gregorius, it's in your hand.

GREGORIUS
So it is.

SELMA
I have news.

ROSALIND
(over her)
Dinner first.

GREGORIUS
(to everyone)
Dinner first!

SELMA
I'm moving to Lisbon.

The knife stops. Gregorius closes the drawer. The trumpet on the radio hits a long, high note, and no one moves.
